   "widgets_values": [
    "## Posed Sprite Sheet: fit a move to a character, render the SCAIL pose frames\n\nExample: the right-hand short uppercut fitted to the example cop. CPU only, no models; about 2 minutes.\n\n1. **Place the inputs**: copy the workflow bundle's `inputs/tracks/` and `inputs/scail_cop/` folders into `ComfyUI/input/`, and load the still `inputs/scail_cop/refs/short_uppercut_side_raw.png` in Load Image (choose file to upload).\n2. **Queue**. Fit Track to Character re-proportions the move's source skeleton to the cop (his DWPose keypoints json); Render SCAIL Cylinders draws the z-buffered cylinder frames; Pad Still to Pose puts the side still on the pose figure's frame-0 box.\n3. **Results** in `ComfyUI/output/pss_example/`: the pose frames + an mp4, and the padded still. They are the pose video and the reference image of the SCAIL-Preview workflow.\n\n**Your own character**: connect the POSE_KEYPOINT output of a DWPose node (comfyui_controlnet_aux) on your front-view picture to `char_keypoints` (it overrides the json path), and read cx / y0 / y1 off your pose frame 0 (or set Pad mode to auto and connect the pose frames).\n\n**The three example moves** (Fit: canvas, hip_x, fixed_shift, pad_top; Render: crop_h, crop_off; Pad: cx, y0, y1, keep_size):\n\n| Move | Fit | Render | Pad (still) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| short uppercut | 1024, 347, false, 0 | 0, -1 | 289, 40, 691, false (short_uppercut_side_raw) |\n| walk | 1024, 347, **true**, 0 | 0, -1 | 249, 28, 679, false (walk_side_raw) |\n| heavy uppercut | 1240, 420, false, 269 | 768, 0 | 284, 200, 737, **true** (short_uppercut_side_raw) |"
   ],
   "title": "Read me"
  }
